From: Cris Sinnott <csinnott@qnx.com>
Subject: [PATCH] whisper.cpp: add cmake_minimum_required upper bound for CMake 4.x compatibility

CMake 4.x requires projects to specify a version range (VERSION X...Y) in
cmake_minimum_required; without an upper bound, CMake 4.0+ applies new policies
that break write_basic_package_version_file's COMPATIBILITY SameMajorVersion.
Add VERSION 3.5...3.31 range to match what ggml's own CMakeLists.txt does.

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -1,4 +1,4 @@
-cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.5) # for add_link_options and implicit target directories.
+cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.5...3.31) # for add_link_options and implicit target directories.
 project("whisper.cpp" C CXX)
 project("whisper.cpp" VERSION 1.9.1)
 include(CheckIncludeFileCXX)
